Lumen has a new visual identity, and its marketing site must carry it through the design system's own theming, not one-off styles on each element. Apply the brand from the data: the brand colour for primary buttons, links and focus rings; a warm stone-grey neutral palette; a 4px corner radius on buttons, inputs, cards and menus; the serif heading font and the sans body font given (both are system fonts, so load nothing); and a dark theme by default with a light/dark toggle in the header that switches the whole site. Build the home page at `/` (a header with the logo text, navigation and the theme toggle; a hero with the tagline and two calls to action; a row of customer logos as text; three feature sections; a footer) and a pricing page at `/pricing` (a monthly/yearly switch that shows yearly prices at two months free, three plan cards with the Team plan highlighted, a feature comparison table, and the FAQ as an accordion), sharing the header and footer.

