Cutline, a browser video editor, editing the project in the data. At `/`, a full-window editor: a top bar with the project name, undo and redo, and an Export button; a media bin listing the media with type icons and durations; a preview area showing the frame at the playhead (draw it as the clip's colour with its title text and a timecode overlay; there is no real video) with play/pause, previous/next frame and a timecode readout; a multi-track timeline below with a time ruler, the four tracks (video, titles, music, voice-over) as labelled rows with mute and lock buttons, clips drawn at their start and length, a draggable playhead, and a zoom control that rescales the ruler and clips. Clicking a clip selects it and shows an inspector panel with its name, start, length, and either opacity and scale (video), text and font size (titles) or volume (audio), all editable and reflected in the timeline. Playing advances the playhead in real time. Export opens a dialog with the presets, an estimated size, and a progress bar once started. On narrow screens the media bin and inspector collapse into tabs or drawers so the preview and timeline stay usable.

