Orbit, an AI assistant workspace for a product team. A shared layout has a sidebar with a New chat button, a thread search, the threads grouped by when they were updated, and the user menu at the bottom; on phones it becomes a drawer. At `/`, a new-chat screen: a greeting, the suggestion chips, and the composer. At `/c/th-3`, the conversation from the data: user and assistant messages, the assistant's SQL rendered as a code block with a copy button, its result as a table, and actions under each assistant message (copy, retry, good/bad). The composer, at the bottom of both screens, is a growing text area with an attach button that adds file chips (removable), a model picker with the three models, and a send button that is disabled while empty; sending appends the user's message and a simulated streamed assistant reply with a stop button. At `/settings`, a settings page with the default model, a custom instructions text area, a theme choice, and data controls (export chats, delete all chats behind a confirmation dialog).

